<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">10062026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran's Revolutionary Guard struck two US bases across the Gulf overnight, hitting the Fifth Fleet in Bahrain and drawing Kuwait's air defenses into the fight, after American forces struck Qeshm island and Sirik directly.</s> <s>The war's flipped from US strikes on Iran to Iranian retaliation reaching every Gulf state that hosts American troops.</s> <s>And in Sirik, US missiles destroyed two village water tanks... cutting drinking water to homes far from any target — though only Iranian and Russian state wires confirm the base strikes.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Ebola's killed one hundred fifteen people across three Congolese provinces, in one of the largest outbreaks ever recorded.</s> <s>The Bundibugyo strain spread undetected for weeks because conflict in Ituri and North Kivu had disabled the very surveillance built to catch it.</s> <s>War degrades the public-health systems that stop epidemics early, so fighting and contagion now compound each other — and the International Rescue Committee is pleading for funds.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli forces killed Jad Suleiman, an eight-year-old boy, in Jabaliya, as the killing in Gaza intensifies while the world watches Iran.</s> <s>One hundred nineteen Palestinians, nineteen of them children, died in May — the deadliest month of this year — and at least forty-six more in June's first nine days.</s> <s>A ceasefire exists on paper, yet the lethal enforcement of the so-called yellow line hasn't stopped the dying.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kenyan police shot a protester dead in Nanyuki on Tuesday, at a site being used to quarantine Americans evacuated from Congo's Ebola outbreak.</s> <s>Kenya has no local cases of its own, yet the US has kept flying equipment in even after a court suspended the project last week.</s> <s>A Kenyan life was lost over a facility the country's own courts had already halted.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>On the day Narendra Modi became India's longest-serving prime minister, a youth movement that began as an online joke filled Delhi's Jantar Mantar.</s> <s>The self-styled cockroaches held their first street rally on the sixth of June, turning a social-media meme into a physical occupation.</s> <s>It's the same template seen from Nepal to Kenya — young people routing around the old opposition parties through internet culture.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Xi Jinping used a summit to treat North Korea as a nuclear-armed state in all but name, framing Kim Jong Un's arsenal as established rather than negotiable.</s> <s>China chairs the very UN body charged with enforcing sanctions on Pyongyang, even as the Security Council still formally rejects its nuclear status.</s> <s>When the enforcer reframes the crime as settled fact, the rule itself quietly dies.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's president, Asif Ali Zardari, has forwarded a heart association's petition for higher taxes on ultra-processed foods to his finance and revenue officials.</s> <s>Taxing junk food is one of the few public-health levers that also raises money, which is why a debt-strained treasury might actually move on it.</s> <s>Whether the food industry's lobbying blunts it, as it has with sugar and tobacco elsewhere, is the open question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Egypt's new tax on state firms, tied to its <sub alias="I M F">IMF</sub> loan, would take five percent of their profits — but hands the prime minister undefined power to grant exemptions.</s> <s>The military's empire of ninety-seven companies is widely expected to seek exactly such an exemption.</s> <s>A reform written to satisfy lenders may end up shielding the most powerful economic actor of all.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>BYD predicts eighty percent of China's car sales will soon be electric, after the country hit a record sixty-three percent in May against just ten percent in the US.</s> <s>China's locking in an electric future and the factories to export it, opening a Hungary plant even as a hundred-percent American tariff walls its cars out.</s> <s>Whoever owns the electric supply chain owns the next two decades of the auto industry.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Germany's Isar Aerospace raised two hundred seventy million euros to scale up rocket production, setting its second Spectrum launch for mid-June.</s> <s>The money buys sovereign launch capacity Europe has lacked, a bet that serial-produced small rockets can close the gap with SpaceX rather than depend on it.</s> <s>Isar's repeatedly slipped timeline shows just how hard that catch-up is — its first flight failed within a minute of liftoff.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Researchers in Cambridge have found that AI trained on known physics can grow too attached to it, blinding itself to discoveries beyond the standard model.</s> <s>Transfer learning slashes the compute cost of searching the cosmos, but it teaches a model to see only what's already predicted.</s> <s>So the team proposes deliberate unlearning — making the machine forget established physics before it goes hunting for the new.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>At Malawi's Dzaleka camp, fifty-two thousand people now shelter in a space built for twelve thousand, as aid collapses around them.</s> <s>World Food Programme support has fallen from one hundred dollars a month per family to just seven, squeezed by shrinking donor budgets and compounding climate disasters.</s> <s>The agency warns it may suspend assistance entirely by the end of June unless donors fill the gap.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Ukraine's AI-guided drones now strike one hundred fifty miles deep into Russian territory, hitting fuel, trucks and trains where cargo concentrates and air defenses thin.</s> <s>The Azov First Corps says the targeting lets a small force reach far beyond the front, disrupting rail lines into Crimea.</s> <s>Artificial intelligence is multiplying the reach of the outgunned — a lesson every smaller military is now studying.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A campaign using fake romantic profiles has been harvesting location data from Russia's frontline soldiers since the summer of last year, a Russian security firm reports.</s> <s>The lures, traced to a group called SiribClone, need no malware at all and resist the usual technical defenses.</s> <s>The oldest trick of espionage, human desire, still beats the newest cybersecurity — even on a digital battlefield.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Amazon engineers nicknamed the company's own mandated coding tool Sloppenheimer in an internal Slack channel obtained by reporters.</s> <s>The very workers ordered to use the AI are the ones quietly documenting where it breaks, in a back channel because the official line is enthusiastic adoption.</s> <s>When a workforce's lived experience diverges this far from the press release, the productivity claims are running ahead of the product.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>